    "image_with_text_dwGeUe": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_73GTKi": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading_text": "Why consulting & site visits matter",
            "heading_size": "h3",
            "enable_h1_tag": false
          }
        },
        "description_zAjXGh": {
          "type": "description",
          "settings": {
            "description_text": "<p>General growing advice isn’t enough for truffles. This crop sits at the intersection of tree physiology, soil chemistry, microbiology, soil biome, irrigation, and climate—and the signals that something’s wrong are often subtle or invisible without the right tests and trained eyes. An ATC consulting engagement—especially when paired with a site visit—helps you:</p><ul><li>See what’s really happening in the orchard, not just what’s visible from the headland.</li><li>Link soil and root test results with what we observe on the ground.</li><li>Compare your orchard’s development and yields against benchmarks from a global network of truffle sites.</li><li>Turn a long learning curve into a structured, science-based improvement plan.</li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "subheading_ftAGjk": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading_text": "We work with three main groups of growers:"
          }
        },
        "description_ELCi63": {
          "type": "description",
          "settings": {
            "description_text": "<ol><li>Truffle orchard owners who have not produced truffles yet.</li><li>Growers who are producing truffles and want to increase yield and the percentage of trees that fruit each season.</li><li>Prospective growers who are considering truffle cultivation.</li></ol>"
          }
        },
        "button_Paqezw": {
          "type": "button",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "button_primary_label": "For Growers",
            "button_primary_style": "secondary",
