    "image_with_text_BMQiPG": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_RCngeY": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading_text": "Consulting for orchards that haven't produced yet",
            "heading_size": "h3",
            "enable_h1_tag": false
          }
        },
        "description_E3wwnN": {
          "type": "description",
          "settings": {
            "description_text": "<p>For non-producing orchards, the central questions are always the same: Is this orchard still on track? If not, why—and what can be done about it? We use site visits and structured analysis to answer those questions honestly and constructively.</p>"
          }
        },
        "subheading_yetk7H": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading_text": "Diagnose what’s holding your orchard back"
          }
        },
        "description_yEAEdH": {
          "type": "description",
          "settings": {
            "description_text": "<p>During a consulting engagement, we review:</p><ul><li>Site fundamentals: climate, layout, drainage, aspect, and exposure.</li><li>Soil status: pH, trace elements, structure, and key nutrients (often via our Soil Analysis Service).</li><li>Root and mycorrhiza health: whether the truffle fungus is present, thriving, or being outcompeted (via Root Analysis where appropriate).</li><li>Orchard management: irrigation patterns, groundcover, pruning, weed control, pests and any past interventions.</li></ul>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_RCngeY",
